class.description:
A [VoxelField] stores a solid as the signed distance to its surface, sampled on a grid. Negative samples are inside the solid, positive samples are outside, and the surface is where the samples cross zero. Storing a solid this way means arbitrary shapes can be added and removed from it with no regard for what was there before, which is what a mesh cannot do. Shapes are added and removed by stamping a [VoxelBrush], and the field re-extracts a mesh from the regions the stamp touched. Attach the field to a [VoxelVolume3D] to see that mesh in a scene. All positions passed to a field are in the field's own space, never the world's. A [VoxelVolume3D] applies its own transform on top, so moving the node does not move anything inside the field. The field itself is only a handle. The data lives in [VoxelServer], and the resource frees it when the resource is freed. [codeblock] var field := VoxelField.new() field.bounds = AABB(Vector3(-0.5, -0.5, -0.5), Vector3.ONE) field.voxel_size = 0.01
var block := VoxelBrushBox.new() block.size = Vector3(0.6, 0.2, 0.4) field.stamp(block, Transform3D(), VoxelField.OP_UNION)
var hole := VoxelBrushSphere.new() hole.radius = 0.05 field.stamp(hole, Transform3D(Basis(), Vector3(0.1, 0, 0)), VoxelField.OP_SUBTRACT) [/codeblock]
